* {{audio|en|en-us-inasmuch.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌtʃ}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{term-label|en|obsolete}} In [[like]] degree; in like manner; to the same or similar degree; [[likewise]]. {{defdate|14<sup>th</sup> c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1848| title=Selections from the Memorabilia of Swedenborg|author=Emanuel Swedenborg | page=| passage=As to what in general respects the life of souls, or spirits lately decease, it was made manifest to me by much experience, that a man, when he comes into another life, does not know that he is in another life, imagining that he is still in the world, yea, in his own body; '''inasmuch''', that when he is informed that he is a spirit, he is filled with wonder and astonishment, as well because he is althogether as a man, as to his senses, desires and thoughts, as from this, that he did not believe, when he lived in the world, that he was a spirit, or (as is the case with some) that a spirit could be such.}}
#* '''1913''', United States. Army Medical Department, ''Bulletin'' (page 109)
#*: It seemed to me that the King was making uncomplimentary remarks about his dead father in the coffin, '''inasmuch''' to say that his father in the coffin was the same kind of man as what people were accusing me of being.

